IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: W.P. (Crl.) No. 532 of 1992
CITATION: (1997) 1 SCC 416
YEAR: 1997

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Kuldip Singh, A.S. Anand

PARTIES:
D.K. Basu vs State of West Bengal

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Constitution of India, Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Article 21, Article 22, Section 50 CrPC, Section 54 CrPC

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
custodial violence, arrest memo, medical examination, mandatory arrest guidelines

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Laid down mandatory guidelines for law enforcement during arrest and interrogation to eliminate custodial deaths and uphold constitutional guarantees under Articles 21 and 22.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Article 21, Article 22, Section 50 CrPC, Section 54 CrPC.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

